#* {{RQ:Hobbes Leviathan|chapter=Of the Signification of Spirit, Angel, and Inspiration in the Books of Holy Scripture|page=212|passage=VVhy therefore may not the Angels that appeared to [[w:Lot (biblical person)|Lot]], {{...}} be underſtood of images of men, ſupernaturally formed in the Fancy; as vvell as before by Angel vvas underſtood a '''fancyed''' Voice?}}
#* {{RQ:Defoe Crusoe 2|page=352|passage=That being depriv'd of all the '''fancy'd''' Felicity vvhich he enjoy'd, in the full Exerciſe of all thoſe Vices, he ſaid, he vvas at leiſure to look upon the dark Side of them, vvhere he found all manner of Deformity, and vvas novv convinc'd, that Virtue only makes a Man truly vviſe, rich and great, and preſerves him in the VVay to a ſuperior Happineſs in a future State.}}
#* {{RQ:Thomson Works|volume=II|title=Ode|section=stanza III|page=220|passage=Oh! if thou hover'ſt round my walk, / While, under ev'ry well-known tree, / I to thy '''fancy'd''' ſhadow talk, / And every tear is full of thee.}}
#* {{RQ:Southey Joan of Arc|lines=903–906|page=362|passage=[S]till by the maid / {{smallcaps|Love}} went submiss, with eye more dangerous / Than '''fancied''' basilisk to wound whoe'er / Too bold approached, {{...}}}}
# [[organize|Organized]], or (especially of [[attire#Noun|attire]]) [[design#Verb|designed]], to suit one's [[fancy#Noun|fancy]] or [[whim#Noun|whim]].
#* {{RQ:Prior Poems|poem=On Exodus 3. 14.|stanza=VI|page=4|passage=Man does vvith dangerous Curioſity / Theſe unfathom'd VVonders try: / VVith '''fancy'd''' Rules and Arbitrary Lavvs / Matter and Motion he reſtrains, / And ſtudy'd Lines and fictious Circles dravvs; {{...}}}}
# [[have#Verb|Having]] a {{l|en|fancy|t=[[inclination]], [[liking#Noun|liking]], or [[love#Noun|love]]}} for; [[desired#Adjective|desired]], [[favourite#Adjective|favourite]].
#* {{RQ:Fuller Joseph|chapter=Faction Confuted|pages=184–185|pageref=185|passage=Now St. [[w:Paul the Apostle|Paul]], "not willing to make" these ministers "a public example," concealeth their persons, yet discovereth the fault; and, making bold with his brethren, {{w|Apollos}} and [[w:Cephas of Iconium|Cephas]], applieth to them and himself what the Corinthians spake of their '''fancied''' preachers. "Now this I say, that every one of you saith, I am of Paul; and I am of Apollos; and I am of Cephas; and I am of Christ."}}
#* {{RQ:Robert Browning Red Cotton|page=245|passage=I did not call him fool, and vex my friend, / But quietly allowed experiment, / Encouraged him to dust his drink, and now / Grate ''lignum vitæ'' now bruise so-called grains / Of Paradise, and now, for perfume, pour / Distilment rare, the rose of Jericho, / Holy-thorn, passion-flower, and what know I? / Till beverage obtained the '''fancied''' smack.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Graham Bean|title=[[w:Scotland national rugby union team|Scotland]] beat [[w:England national rugby union team|England]] at Twickenham for the first time in 38 years|newspaper={{w|The Scotsman}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220710041336/https://www.scotsman.com/sport/rugby-union/scotland-beat-england-twickenham-first-time-38-years-3126677|archivedate=10 July 2022|location=Edinburgh|publisher=The Scotsman Publications, [[w:JPIMedia|JPIMedia Publishing]]|date=6 February 2021|issn=0307-5850|oclc=868238067|passage=The visitors were worthy winners, taking the game to the highly '''fancied''' hosts from the first minute.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Designed in an [[artistic]] [[manner#Noun|manner]].
#* {{RQ:Tatler|author=Steele|issue=142|date=7 March 1710|page=331|passage=His seals are curiously '''fancied''', and exquisitely well cut, and of great use to encourage young gentlemen to write a good hand.}}
#* {{RQ:Burney Cecilia|volume=I|chapter=A Sketch of High Life|page=51|passage=[T]hey have taken thoſe beautiful buckles out of her ſhoes! {{...}} I vvonder vvho'll buy them. I aſſure you they vvere the prettieſt '''fancied''' I ever ſavv.}}

